# Never sent to the Docker daemon as part of this image's build context.
# See lessons/02-dockerfiles-layers-and-caching.md's ".dockerignore"
# section.

# The single most important line in this file: a locally-installed
# node_modules can be tens or hundreds of megabytes, is host-OS-specific
# (some packages here compile or select native binaries per platform --
# see the Dockerfile's own explanation of the win32 binding packages),
# and gets reinstalled fresh, correctly, for Linux, inside the build
# anyway. Sending it as part of the build context would be slow and
# pointless at best, and could ship the wrong platform's native binaries
# into the image at worst.
node_modules

# A previous local build's output -- this image produces its own dist/
# fresh, inside the build; an old one lying around locally has no
# business being copied in.
dist

.git/
.gitignore
*.log
